## 1. Executive Summary

### Problem Statement

Early-stage founders raising on SAFEs and convertibles model dilution in fragile Excel sheets or hit paywalls the moment they try “what happens if my cap goes to $X, I take $Y new money, and top up the pool to Z% post-money?” OpenCap Lite is a self-hosted OSS cap table and transparent scenario engine that gives founders Carta-grade modeling for $0 — every calculation step visible, every assumption editable, no premium tier.

### Success Metrics (12-month)

|Metric                    |Target                                       |Measurement                                                  |
|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
|Active self-hosters       |50                                           |Opt-in anonymous telemetry ping (`POST /telemetry/heartbeat`)|
|Accelerator adoption      |≥1 program recommends it in cohort curriculum|Qualitative confirmation                                     |
|GitHub stars              |500+                                         |Proxy, not a goal                                            |
|Critical-path bug reports |< 3/quarter after v1.0                       |GitHub issues labeled `math-correctness`                     |
|Golden-file test pass rate|100%                                         |CI gate                                                      |

### Non-Goals

- Not a legal automation platform (no document generation, e-signing, or filing workflows)
- Not a tax filing platform (no 83(b), QSBS, or 409A automation)
- Not a full Carta clone (no equity plan administration, ASC 718 expensing, or secondary markets)
- Not an incorporation tool
- Not a data room / investor update platform
- Not going to support US-only conventions forever (currency/jurisdiction pluggable from day 1)

