## 5. User Stories

### Happy Path

- As Priya, I want to create a company, add two founders with their equity grants, and see a clean ownership summary — so I have a baseline cap table.
- As Priya, I want to enter two outstanding SAFEs (one cap-only, one cap+discount) and one convertible note, then create a scenario modeling a $2M seed round at $8M pre-money — so I can see my dilution before signing the term sheet.
- As Priya, I want to change the pre-money valuation and new money amount and see the ownership table update live — so I can negotiate with actual numbers.
- As Priya, I want to see *why* each SAFE chose cap or discount for conversion — so I trust the output.
- As Priya, I want to duplicate a scenario and change one parameter — so I can compare outcomes side by side.
- As Priya, I want to export the final ownership table as CSV — so I can share with my cofounder or lawyer.

### Edge Cases

- As Priya, I want to see a warning (not a hard block) if a note’s maturity date has passed — so I can decide whether to force conversion or repay.
- As Priya, I want MFN SAFEs to be flagged as unresolved — so I don’t make decisions on phantom numbers.
- As Priya, I want to be warned if the scenario exceeds authorized shares — so I know a board action is needed.
- As Priya, I want the system to refuse nonsensical inputs (negative share counts, >100% pool) with a specific error — so I can’t silently build a broken model.

### Non-Technical Deploy

- As Sam, I want to click a “Deploy to Railway” button in the README and have a working instance within 10 minutes — so I don’t need to learn Docker to use this.
- As Sam, I want a hosted read-only demo to try before I deploy — so I can evaluate without commitment.

