## 12. Security & Non-Functional

### Security (v1.0)

- Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with credentials provider by default; email/OTP provider optional
- Multi-company access: any authenticated user sees all companies on the instance (single-tenant model)
- All mutations go through server-side routes; no direct client DB access
- Environment-variable-based secrets (no defaults in Dockerfile)
- CSRF protection via Next.js defaults
- Rate limiting: 60 requests/min per IP on mutation routes (configurable)

### Non-functional targets

- Cold-start `docker compose up` → app reachable in < 60 seconds
- Scenario calculation (up to 20 SAFEs + 5 notes) < 500ms on a 2-core VM
- Page load (main dashboard) < 1.5s on cable
- Zero external network dependencies at runtime (no CDN-hosted fonts, no analytics)

### Accessibility

- All interactive elements keyboard-reachable
- Form inputs labeled via `aria-label` or `<label>`
- Color-contrast WCAG AA
- No “accessibility compliance” claim — aim for AA, document gaps

